    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the frai CLI's gate command. The issue was that when running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was being consumed by the top-level `frai` command (which has `--ci` defined as an option), so it never reached the gate handler.\n\n**The fix:** Modified the gate command handler in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/pilot-haiku-core/with/t1-flag-bug/r1/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 752-753) to capture all remaining arguments from `process.argv` after the 'gate' command, rather than relying only on the parsed `args` array from Commander.\n\n**Key changes:**\n- Added: `const gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');`\n- Added: `const allArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];`\n- Updated the spawnSync call to use `allArgs` instead of `args`\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\u2705 `frai gate init` (without --ci) still works correctly and only creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n\u2705 Package rebuilt successfully with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
